gf-three vfx: attribution

The parameter vocabulary of presets.js and sim.js (size, speed, life, drag, gravity, stretch, blending, emitter shapes
point | sphere | disc | ring | box | line, outward, spin, grow, hueJitter) and the starting numbers of a few presets
(spark-burst, impact-flash, smoke-puff, dust-kick, fire) follow OpenDCAI/GameFactory-3A,
engine_adapters/three_js/plugin/A3GamePlayable/src/engine/vfx-kit.js (pinned: commit 41445aaf3f66d1e5dabde079c9b5eaf04884f68c),
Copyright 2026 OpenDCAI, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
No source code was copied: the simulation and the drawing are written for this kit (an instanced-quad path that runs
on the WebGL and the WebGPU renderer alike; vfx-kit draws with a GLSL ShaderMaterial, which the WebGPU renderer cannot).
That file in turn names the three.quarks (MIT) and Three-VFX (MIT) libraries as the source of its vocabulary.

The three sprites in standin/ (glow.png, puff.png, dot.png) are generated by research/gf-three/tools/make-vfx-standins.mjs
from formulas: no third-party art (CC0-1.0).
